Subject: virtio/fs: a request queue per vCPU, inline opens and ioctls

Every request queue shared one mutex, and the device offered one request
queue, so file requests from all vCPUs were processed one at a time: ten
parallel unzips onto a share ran one request at a time, with one thread
busy and the vCPUs waiting. Offer up to 16 request queues
(set_request_queues, usually one per vCPU; the guest maps CPUs to queues),
each with its own lock, and drain the queue the guest names in KAT_FS_DRAIN.

A bounded open handed every open to a helper thread, usually parked, so an
open cost a thread wakeup on top of the syscall (24 us of host time per
OPEN, most of PHP's per-request file cost without opcache). Try the open on
the calling thread first, with materializing of dataless files turned off
for that thread and O_NONBLOCK so a FIFO cannot block; only what fails or
is not a regular file or directory goes to a helper as before.

FUSE_IOCTL ran on the worker pool although every server answers it at once;
the guest sends one for each isatty() on a shared file (perl, Python).

SETATTR of times by path opened the file to futimens it; utimensat with
AT_SYMLINK_NOFOLLOW does the same in one call.

KATAMARAN_FS_STATS=1 also logs request counts and host time per opcode.

